{
  "group": "shipped JSON schemas",
  "description": "Hand-written conformance cases for the shipped JSON schemas that carry JUDGEMENT — why a constraint matters, or where the shape/meaning split lies. Each schema covered here gets an instance that must be ACCEPTED (which also serves as the seed for the generated tier) and instances that must be REJECTED, naming the constraint that did it.\n\nSCOPE, measured rather than claimed: run `make mutation` for the current per-schema coverage table, `make mutation MUTATION_ARGS=--holes` for any constraint still pinned by nothing, and `--inert` for the keyword occurrences that restrict nothing and are therefore not in the denominator. These hand-written cases pin a small fraction on their own; the mechanical remainder is generated into 11-schema-constraints.json, and the two tiers together are what the sweep measures. Do not trust a percentage written here — the numbers move with every schema edit, which is why the command is given instead of its last answer.\n\nREAD THE SWEEP'S LAST TWO LINES, not just the TOTAL. A schema with NO cases is excluded from the denominator rather than counted as uncovered, so the TOTAL can read 100% while a schema is pinned by nothing at all. As of the v0.5.0 state machine, five of the fifteen shipped schemas are in that position: acs-skill, result, run, step-state and workflow — four of them the new run/step machines' own documents. They are a real gap, not a covered surface.\n\nValidated by runner/jsonschema_mini.py, a stdlib subset validator. It raises on any keyword it does not implement rather than silently passing, so a schema that grows one fails loudly.\n\nThere is no XML here to exclude any more: schemas/acs-messages.xsd and the plugin's validate_xml.py were both removed in v0.5.0 (ADR-0100). What a subagent returns is checked in acs_lib.lifecycle.validate_message, and the documents a step writes are the JSON this dataset covers.",
  "surface": "schemas/*.json",
  "covers": [
    "MAR-527",
    "MAR-530",
    "ADR-0097",
    "ADR-0099"
  ],
  "profile": "bare",
  "cases": [
